{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core","id":1052082,"title":"I finally got hardcopy of Vampire: The Requiem 2e (also CofD core)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-20T12:00:00-08:00","id":1052082,"title":"I finally got hardcopy of Vampire: The Requiem 2e (also CofD core)","content":"And the book is so shiny and pretty, I'm almost afraid to use it.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to having this to use when running Vampire, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:07:52-08:00","id":1052089,"title":"","content":"Hey person who is also in Seattle who I actually probably know, honestly -<br /> <br /> I know how you feel. When I got my premium hardcover of B&amp;S back in 2013, I didn't touch it for like, a year. I only used the pdf. Because I'm weird and it was so pretty.<br /> <br /> I just ordered the new CofD core (in premium!!) because I've been making due with the God Machine Rules Update for a while and I decided it was time to get the real deal. I can't wait for it to come. I also got Dark Eras ordered (in premium because otherwise it would probably fall apart) so I'm super excited.<br /> <br /> I love books!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:23:44-08:00","id":1052103,"title":"","content":"I'm not in Seattle yet so it's at least possible that we don't know each other. I have spent more time in Seattle over the past year than ever before, though. Which isn't saying a lot.<br /> <br /> I should be living there soon.<br /> <br /> And the CofD core is great too. I do like the layout, art, etc. a lot and OBS does a great job with POD products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:28:32-08:00","id":1052107,"title":"","content":"Oh whoops. I remember you mentioning something about how you're from Seattle in another thread I was lurking in or something, so I thought 'you know, I probably know that guy.' Guess I spoke too soon.<br /> <br /> I'm so excited. I've been going on a bit of a 2e book buying spree over the past month. I've got B&amp;S (which is fundamentally unchanged from Vampire 2e so I haven't bothered buying the new version,) Werewolf 2e, Mage 2e, and Promethean 2e, and CofD core and Dark Eras are coming. I also bought all of the anthology books.<br /> <br /> Which is honestly more games than I will ever have time to run, but I love books!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","user":"RomulusGloriosus","date":".  syntax 02-20-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:32:19-08:00","id":1052156,"title":"","content":"Hey, Seattle was where I played Requiem LARP in college! (Well... Olympia, actually, but I went to a few Cam games in Seattle). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a>, do you happen to know Tim Alexander? Used to play Zedikaiah Hoyle in Camarilla Requiem LARP (or maybe still does, I haven't kept up with the LARP scene since I moved back to Colorado)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:43:06-08:00","id":1052163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052156#post1052156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Seattle was where I played Requiem LARP in college! (Well... Olympia, actually, but I went to a few Cam games in Seattle). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a>, do you happen to know Tim Alexander? Used to play Zedikaiah Hoyle in Camarilla Requiem LARP (or maybe still does, I haven't kept up with the LARP scene since I moved back to Colorado)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, actually, but a quick facebook search shows we have mutual friends, which isn't surprising.<br /> <br /> I try and avoid the LARP circuit, because I prefer to tabletop. I did Masquerade LARP for a bit in Seattle, which is how I ended up meeting a lot of the Seattle WW/OPP fans, but I just like tabletopping so much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:47:09-08:00","id":1052166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052163#post1052163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't, actually, but a quick facebook search shows we have mutual friends, which isn't surprising.<br /> <br /> I try and avoid the LARP circuit, because I prefer to tabletop. I did Masquerade LARP for a bit in Seattle, which is how I ended up meeting a lot of the Seattle WW/OPP fans, but I just like tabletopping so much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Tim was the Storyteller for the long-running troupe LARP game I played in back then. We probably have some mutual friends in the area, but I doubt you and I would have come across each other. Anyway, sorry for the derail, I just get excited when the possibility of encouraging old friends on these boards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:44:42-08:00","id":1052201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052107#post1052107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh whoops. I remember you mentioning something about how you're from Seattle in another thread I was lurking in or something, so I thought 'you know, I probably know that guy.' Guess I spoke too soon.<br /> <br /> I'm so excited. I've been going on a bit of a 2e book buying spree over the past month. I've got B&amp;S (which is fundamentally unchanged from Vampire 2e so I haven't bothered buying the new version,) Werewolf 2e, Mage 2e, and Promethean 2e, and CofD core and Dark Eras are coming. I also bought all of the anthology books.<br /> <br /> Which is honestly more games than I will ever have time to run, but I love books!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Well I'm not a guy so that's another strike. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:47:44-08:00","id":1052204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052201#post1052201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Well I'm not a guy so that's another strike. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am just not doing well today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:35:17-08:00","id":1052231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core#post1052082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the book is so shiny and pretty, I'm almost afraid to use it.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to having this to use when running Vampire, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whelp, when I got mine I was almost afraid to touch it! It was my first PoD book and I didn't know how good the materials would be (but my copy is in almost pristine conditions, so, good).<br /> I have Blood and Smoke and not VtR 2e, though... it almost feels like I have some kind of rarity in my hands, even if I know it isn't.<br /> I love B&amp;S cover just as much as the &quot;canon&quot; VtR one. It feels so in theme, but in a different, more malincholic way.<br /> EDIT: It sucks not having in index, though. Well, I got the pdf for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:43:55-08:00","id":1052238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052231#post1052231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whelp, when I got mine I was almost afraid to touch it! It was my first PoD book and I didn't know how good the materials would be (but my copy is in almost pristine conditions, so, good).<br /> I have Blood and Smoke and not VtR 2e, though... it almost feels like I have some kind of rarity in my hands, even if I know it isn't.<br /> I love B&amp;S cover just as much as the &quot;canon&quot; VtR one. It feels so in theme, but in a different, more malincholic way.<br /> EDIT: It sucks not having in index, though. Well, I got the pdf for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love the Blood and Smoke cover so much. It's so thematic. I feel like it really fits VtR 2e much better than the original Hand-with-Rose-Petals does, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:21:28-08:00","id":1052255,"title":"","content":"I also think the VTR 2e hardcover is pretty and am from Seattle! (Sort of, from the South End and now live on the East Side).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""}