ts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:34:04-08:00","id":1052264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052259#post1052259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eastside definitely counts as Seattle, even if most folks from the Eastside would get hives from that sentence. My fiancee and I live downtown but she works in Bellevue, so life is life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly don't count it as Seattle, any more than I do Renton or Everett. I do understand that outside the state though Seattle basically means Western Washington.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:40:21-08:00","id":1052268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052264#post1052264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly don't count it as Seattle, any more than I do Renton or Everett. I do understand that outside the state though Seattle basically means Western Washington.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everett's a little far to consider Seattle, imo, but I'd consider Shoreline, Lynnwood, and even Renton to be &quot;Seattle.&quot; But folks who live outside of the city tend to try and distance themselves from the city, and I get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:28:37-08:00","id":1052290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052156#post1052156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Seattle was where I played Requiem LARP in college! (Well... Olympia, actually, but I went to a few Cam games in Seattle). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a>, do you happen to know Tim Alexander? Used to play Zedikaiah Hoyle in Camarilla Requiem LARP (or maybe still does, I haven't kept up with the LARP scene since I moved back to Colorado)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in Portland, OR Camarilla-wise but played in Seattle and nearby areas many times. But that was in the mid-late 90s. I think I stopped larping in 2000 or 2001.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:30:55-08:00","id":1052292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052259#post1052259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry for making this post about Seattle because I'm a weirdo lurker! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Eastside definitely counts as Seattle, even if most folks from the Eastside would get hives from that sentence. My fiancee and I live downtown but she works in Bellevue, so life is life.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries about bringing up Seattle, since I'll be living there soon, will be running Requiem there and the Requiem game itself will be set in Carthian-run Seattle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052231#post1052231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whelp, when I got mine I was almost afraid to touch it! It was my first PoD book and I didn't know how good the materials would be (but my copy is in almost pristine conditions, so, good).<br /> I have Blood and Smoke and not VtR 2e, though... it almost feels like I have some kind of rarity in my hands, even if I know it isn't.<br /> I love B&amp;S cover just as much as the &quot;canon&quot; VtR one. It feels so in theme, but in a different, more malincholic way.<br /> EDIT: It sucks not having in index, though. Well, I got the pdf for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood &amp; Smoke cover is pretty great and I might have ordered it if it was kept as up to date as Requiem 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:50:39-08:00","id":1052300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052292#post1052292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries about bringing up Seattle, since I'll be living there soon, will be running Requiem there and the Requiem game itself will be set in Carthian-run Seattle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet. If you're ever looking for folks at your table, my fiancee and I have been playing Requiem forever and are always looking for new games. I've actually got an on-again off-again game set in Carthian-run Seattle too. Something about the Emerald City just jives with the Movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:53:52-08:00","id":1052302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052290#post1052290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was in Portland, OR Camarilla-wise but played in Seattle and nearby areas many times. But that was in the mid-late 90s. I think I stopped larping in 2000 or 2001.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we had like... a 10 year gap, I started in 2010, stopped in 2013.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:56:24-08:00","id":1052303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052264#post1052264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly don't count it as Seattle, any more than I do Renton or Everett. I do understand that outside the state though Seattle basically means Western Washington.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an odd phenomenon. I remember telling people I was going to school in Olympia, they'd have no idea what I was talking about, despite it being the capital, and I'd have to explain it was like a two hour drive south of Seattle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:39:28-08:00","id":1052332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052303#post1052303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an odd phenomenon. I remember telling people I was going to school in Olympia, they'd have no idea what I was talking about, despite it being the capital, and I'd have to explain it was like a two hour drive south of Seattle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of the same thing with New York City and Albany, or Harrisburg and Philadelphia (or Pittsburgh for that matter.) A lot of state capitals were either a big deal and got overshadowed, or were strategically placed because a lot of people who don't live in The City resent The City. (Doesn't matter where The City is, it's The City.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:01:43-08:00","id":1052575,"title":"","content":"We also have the problem of the State name being taken by DC, so you can't just say Washington without people (especially east-coasters) assuming you mean DC. So it just becomes Seattle for the whole area.<br /> <br /> I was once at a concert at the Gorge (on the other side of the Cascade Mountains) and the band said &quot;Hello Seattle!&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:39:57-08:00","id":1052585,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it such a great idea to rename Columbia to Washington to avoid being mixed up with the District of Columbia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:57:27-08:00","id":1052589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052575#post1052575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also have the problem of the State name being taken by DC, so you can't just say Washington without people (especially east-coasters) assuming you mean DC. So it just becomes Seattle for the whole area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is interesting in itself because nobody that lives in the DC area calls it Washington. Its just DC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:20:24-08:00","id":1052600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052589#post1052589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is interesting in itself because nobody that lives in the DC area calls it Washington. Its just DC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nobody I've ever met, anywhere, period, in the US calls Washington, DC, Washington. It's always DC. But still, having grown up on the East Coast (Philadelphia area) Washington State is still called Washington State for good measure. Never once have I heard it called &quot;Seattle&quot; - though really, the only place in Washington State that ever gets mentioned outside of Washington State is Seattle. MAYBE Spokane, and it's always pronounced wrong.<br /> <br /> BACK ON ACTUAL TOPIC, I just got my CofD Core and Dark Eras premium hardcovers yesterday. The Dark Eras book is like a textbook. It's MASSIVE. I'm so glad I got it in premium because I'm fairly certain a standard would fall apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:33:25-08:00","id":1052630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052600#post1052600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BACK ON ACTUAL TOPIC, I just got my CofD Core and Dark Eras premium hardcovers yesterday. The Dark Eras book is like a textbook. It's MASSIVE. I'm so glad I got it in premium because I'm fairly certain a standard would fall apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>My girlfriend asked me what it was I had against spiders when she saw my Kickstarter copy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:29:19-08:00","id":1054011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1052302#post1052302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we had like... a 10 year gap, I started in 2010, stopped in 2013.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured it'd be something like that.<br /> <br /> I've been tempted to start larping again once I move to Seattle, but then I worry about making my gaming schedule <i>too</i> full.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":".  wth brain 02-23-2017, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:48:27-08:00","id":1054024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1054011#post1054011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I figured it'd be something like that.<br /> <br /> I've been tempted to start larping again once I move to Seattle, but then I worry about making my gaming schedule <i>too</i> full.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the organized LARP community in Washington is pretty toxic. I got lucky in meeting a guy at my first Cam game who was part of a large group of friends who had done a lot of Masquerade LARP as an independent troup years back. He invited me to a private game which was only like four other people at the time, but it went so well he contacted his old group's ST (Tim, who I mentioned earlier) and convinced him to come out of LARP retirement to run a game, and all of their old friends rallied to him. Plus I brought in a ton of new blood for them from the college's gaming club, so they expanded and were able to keep it going for a few years until it fell apart due to various outside factors. It was just a matter of the right place, right time. Every time I tried to branch out into Cam games it was an awful experience. Except the Forsaken game, but that was entirely made up of players from the troupe game, and it later turned out that the guy who was STing it hadn't been getting proper approvals for any of his gonzo plot, and eventually the whole venue had to be nuked. Weird times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-23-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T18:48:06-08:00","id":1054144,"title":"","content":"Toxic? Ugh. I'm sorry to hear that. It wasn't so bad in the 90s. I wonder how many people from then are still around.<br /> <br /> Sounds like your private game went pretty well, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T19:09:03-08:00","id":1054148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1054144#post1054144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toxic? Ugh. I'm sorry to hear that. It wasn't so bad in the 90s. I wonder how many people from then are still around.<br /> <br /> Sounds like your private game went pretty well, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, everybody in the troup assured me it was a Washington Camarilla specific thing, and that the Camarilla was much better elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:13:26-08:00","id":1054495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1054148#post1054148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, everybody in the troup assured me it was a Washington Camarilla specific thing, and that the Camarilla was much better elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>every LARP I've ever been a part of was toxic...I fully believe that there are places where it's fun and healthy and safe, but every LARP I've ever been in has been full of abusive problem players, often older men taking advantage of impressionable young women, and people who simply cannot gender correctly for the life of them even after a year of roleplaying together. It is why I steer closer to tabletops than LARPs, just because tabletopping tends to be more personal and less full of conflict, but I, once again, fully believe that this does not apply to EVERY LARP ever. I'm just not sure I want to give it a chance anymore....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T03:30:06-08:00","id":1054696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1054148#post1054148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, everybody in the troup assured me it was a Washington Camarilla specific thing, and that the Camarilla was much better elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played in LARPs from Seattle, WA to Houston, TX - mostly in Oregon - and I think most LARPs have issues, at least in the Camarilla. There are problems mentioned in the previous post, but also people vying for as much power as possible, people using the game as a means to channel their nastiness (there are nearly always players whose participation brings the game down). <i>Despite</i> all that, I had a lot of fun LARPing when I did, but if someone's specifically calling a city out as toxic, that's worrisome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:30:55-08:00","id":1054797,"title":"","content":"So many things to reply to... lol<br /> <br /> First, to be on-topic, yeah, the books are pretty nice. I kinda don't want to run Forsaken because my book is nice and pristine and I don't want to mess it up. I ran a lot of Forsaken in the Cam, and my book got...well-loved, let's say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second, apparently I need to move to Seattle, what with all the folks around there.<br /> <br /> Third...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of the same thing with New York City and Albany, or Harrisburg and Philadelphia (or Pittsburgh for that matter.) A lot of state capitals were either a big deal and got overshadowed, or were strategically placed because a lot of people who don't live in The City resent The City. (Doesn't matter where The City is, it's The City.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in the Harrisburg area, and while I've never heard it associated with Philly or Pittsburgh, that wouldn't surprise me. Pretty sure some folks think Philly is the state capital.<br /> <br /> And fourth...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I tried to branch out into Cam games it was an awful experience. Except the Forsaken game, but that was entirely made up of players from the troupe game, and it later turned out that the guy who was STing it hadn't been getting proper approvals for any of his gonzo plot, and eventually the whole venue had to be nuked. Weird times.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm entirely biased, having served as EC ARST Forsaken twice, AMST Forsaken twice, and AAMST Forsaken at least once (if not twice...wow, sensing a theme here), I have to high-five the praise for Forsaken. It was a good community by-and-large, I thought. I don't recall having to nuke a venue, though....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:22:23-08:00","id":1054829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1052082-i-finally-got-hardcopy-of-vampire-the-requiem-2e-also-cofd-core?p=1054797#post1054797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm entirely biased, having served as EC ARST Forsaken twice, AMST Forsaken twice, and AAMST Forsaken at least once (if not twice...wow, sensing a theme here), I have to high-five the praise for Forsaken. It was a good community by-and-large, I thought. I don't recall having to nuke a venue, though....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's come up before and it occured after you had gotten out of the Cam scene. If I recall correctly, it happened in like 2012 or 13.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedb